‎[ 04 — THE PLAYBOOK.]
‎
‎*The Stoic Survivor*
‎
‎Before building any new channel, ask four questions:
‎
‎1. What am I moving?
‎
‎Knowledge? Trust? Money? Ideas?
‎
‎2. What infrastructure carries it?
‎
‎Physical? Digital? Financial? Social?
‎
‎3. Where does friction still exist?
‎
‎Visibility? Access? Cost? Distance? Trust?
‎
‎4. If one route disappeared tomorrow, could the journey continue another way?
‎
‎Robust systems are rarely dependent on a single path, the operator who maps their routes before they need them is the operator who keeps delivering when others stop.
‎
‎The Rule:
‎
‎Rule #9: Movement is universal. Infrastructure determines how far value can travel. Ownership determines who benefits when it arrives.
‎
‎Arc 01 revealed the terrain. Arc 02 built the foundation. Arc 03 sets the cargo in motion.
